# Optional. Copy this file to .env.test to point the test suite at a
# different database than your local dev Postgres - e.g. a separate
# database (or Neon branch) on a hosted provider, if local Postgres setup
# is more trouble than it's worth. Never commit .env.test.
#
# If this file doesn't exist, tests fall back to a local
# `issueflow_test` database automatically (see tests/setup.ts).
#
# Use a database SEPARATE from your main dev DATABASE_URL - the test
# suite freely creates and deletes rows. Neon requires sslmode=require,
# and migrations should run against Neon's *direct* (non-pooled)
# connection string, not the pooled one - Prisma's migration engine
# doesn't play well with connection pooling.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@your-neon-host.neon.tech/issueflow_test?sslmode=require"
